{"id": 29, "ts": 1780468583.4645402, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**.\u202fBuilding on Sarah\u2019s recent note that C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d we now have concrete evidence of crew\u2011cooperation potential, which directly addresses one of the biggest concerns we have with Candidate\u202fD\u2019s \u201chot temper\u201d and \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d perception.\u202fC also demonstrates strong decision\u2011making \u2013 \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d and \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d \u2013 and solid technical competence (\u201cunderstands complicated technology\u201d), all of which are critical for long\u2011distance operations.\u202fWhile C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric reputation are not ideal, the positive cockpit atmosphere suggests these issues may be manageable, especially compared with D\u2019s temperament risk that could more readily disrupt crew coordination.\u202fThus, C\u2019s blend of reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and now demonstrated crew\u2011interaction strength makes him the stronger overall fit at this point."}
