{"id": 45, "ts": 1780468779.9139907, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s reliability and stress handling, but the lack of any concrete examples of B\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, leadership, or decision\u2011making in safety\u2011critical situations is a serious gap.\u202fWithout evidence that B can effectively coordinate with a co\u2011pilot or lead the crew during an emergency, we cannot be confident he meets the crew\u2011cooperation and decision\u2011quality criteria that are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul flights.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC does have documented evidence of a positive cockpit atmosphere, which directly demonstrates crew\u2011cooperation, and we also know he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d and is \u201c100\u202f% reliable.\u201d\u202fThese strengths address reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and crew interaction\u2014all core to our role.\u202fWhile C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric reputation are concerns, they appear less likely to jeopardize safety than the temperament risks we see with Candidate\u202fD (hot temper, know\u2011it\u2011all perception) and the complete lack of crew\u2011cooperation evidence for B.\nGiven the current evidence, I am shifting my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
